BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Zero-Waste Drop-Off Event & More!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260523T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260524T000000
DTSTAMP:20260729T080830Z
UID:08dffccb-c17a-544d-8a5f-2084e959d1d0
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, May 23\, 2026 / 10 am to 4 pm & Indoor activities: 
 10:30 am to 3:30 pm.\n\nHeld in partnership with the (https://burlingtonce
 ntre.ca/sustainability/) Burlington Centre and (https://techgenius.ca/) Te
 ch Genius Burlington Inc\, we’re excited to host another impactful event
  at the Burlington Centre’s convenient parking area (corner of Guelph Li
 ne & Fairview) to accept computer and cell phone electronics.\n\nDiscover 
 below how you can further grow the impact of these events by organizing co
 llections with your networks!\n\nThere’s more. A series of (https://shop
 .terracycle.com/en-CA) Terracycle Zero Waste (https://chopvalue.com/en-ca?
 srsltid=AfmBOoqeso5s1WdcIgiSNQdM9XjR6CSPw6VXZGsllncMOkznzBFacN8p.) bins ar
 e also on site to accept more unique waste items not currently accepted in
  Halton Region’s recycling program. And you can even drop off wooden cho
 psticks to the (https://chopvalue.com/en-ca?srsltid=AfmBOoqeso5s1WdcIgiSNQ
 dM9XjR6CSPw6VXZGsllncMOkznzBFacN8p.) ChopValue bin we will have available 
 at the event.\n\nAfter dropping off your items outside\, come inside betwe
 en 10:30 AM and 3:30 PM to explore our interactive Towards Zero Waste spac
 e. Families can enjoy games and hands-on activities for all ages\, while a
 dults and youth can dive deeper into solutions.\n\nAn optional suggested d
 onation of $5 will be gratefully accepted to advance our work – and free
  pollinator-friendly wildflower seed packets are available!\n\n(https://ww
 w.burlingtongreen.org/programs/zero-waste-events/) LEARN MORE HERE!\nURL: 
 https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/zero-waste-drop-off-event-more/
URL:https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/zero-waste-drop-off-event-more/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Spring Events!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260301T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260531T000000
DTSTAMP:20260729T080832Z
UID:29c78515-802b-5e21-b75e-2c911e197ba3
DESCRIPTION:We’re excited to share a (https://www.burlingtongreen.org/sp
 ring-into-action/) terrific lineup of inclusive opportunities for Burlingt
 on residents\, youth\, groups\, and businesses to have fun and help the pl
 anet locally.\n\nCity-wide clean ups\, community tree planting\, Earth Mon
 th activities\, a variety of volunteer opportunities\, a zero waste extrav
 aganza\, a native plant sale\, and more.\n\nTogether we can take action on
  climate change and make a difference for a cleaner\, greener Burlington.\
 n\n(https://www.burlingtongreen.org/spring-into-action/) Spring into ACTIO
 N with BurlingtonGreen!\n\n(https://www.burlingtongreen.org/spring-into-ac
 tion/)\n\nOpportunities supported by the City of Burlington plus community
  sponsors\n\n(https://www.burlington.ca/en/home-property-and-environment/e
 nvironment.aspx)\nURL: https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/spring-event
 s/
URL:https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/spring-events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Inspiring Evening with David Suzuki & Tara Cullis!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260308T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260309T000000
DTSTAMP:20260729T080831Z
UID:4c6fd260-75a1-5e15-b869-d7280969b7b5
DESCRIPTION:David Suzuki and Tara Cullis are coming to the Burlington Perf
 orming Arts Centre (BPAC) on March 8th\, and BurlingtonGreen is proud to b
 e a partner for this special event.\n\n(https://burlingtonpac.ca/events/wh
 at-you-wont-do-for-love/) What You Won’t Do For Love is a special event 
 that is expected to sell out.\n\nJoin us for a powerful opportunity to gat
 her\, reflect\, and feel inspired by voices that have shaped environmental
  action for decades.\n\nSPECIAL OFFER: (https://www.burlingtongreen.org/ne
 wsletter-signup/) Sign up to receive BurlingtonGreen’s popular e-newslet
 ter\, and you’ll receive a promo code for 25% off your tickets. (while t
 ickets remain available)\n\nYou can also purchase tickets https://burlingt
 onpac.ca/events/what-you-wont-do-for-love/\, while seats remain.\n\n(https
 ://burlingtonpac.ca/events/what-you-wont-do-for-love/)\n\n(https://burling
 tonpac.ca/events/what-you-wont-do-for-love/) EVENT TICKETS\n\nWhat others 
 are saying:\n\n“A deeply personal\, totally enchanting love story. David
  and Tara take us on a magical journey into the heart of commitment – to
  one another\, to family\, to community\, to justice and to the planet. A 
 testament to hope.”\n\n– Maude Barlow (Author and activist\, founding 
 member of the Council of Canadians\, co-founder of the Blue Planet Project
 )\n\n“Warm\, wise and overflowing with generosity\, this is a love story
  so epic it embraces all of creation. Yet another reminder of how blessed 
 we are to be in the struggle with elders like David and Tara.”\n\n– Na
 omi Klein (author\, journalist\, social activist\, and filmmaker) and Avi 
 Lewis (filmmaker\, climate activist\, educator)\nURL: https://www.burlingt
 ongreen.org/events/an-inspiring-evening-with-david-suzuki-tara-cullis/
URL:https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/an-inspiring-evening-with-david
 -suzuki-tara-cullis/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Green Up Community Tree Planting Event
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260502T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260503T000000
DTSTAMP:20260729T080830Z
UID:6eb4f6d1-ace3-5a16-b7ee-a43cde3c391c
DESCRIPTION:Let’s Grow Burlington’s Tree Canopy Together!\n\nBurlingto
 nGreen and City of Burlington Forestry staff are organizing a community tr
 ee planting to take place from 9:30 am to noon on Saturday\, September 26\
 , 2026\, at a location to be announced this summer.\n\nTogether we will pl
 ant 500+ native trees PLUS some lucky participants will each win a beautif
 ul tree to plant at their Burlington homes!\n\nSpace is limited for this p
 opular event.\n\n(https://www.burlingtongreen.org/newsletter-signup/) Sign
  up to receive our popular monthly eco-newsletter\, which will include not
 ifications about when registration will open for this event.\n\nCheck out 
 our fabulous line-up of (https://www.burlingtongreen.org/donate/sponsorshi
 p-opportunities/) sponsorship opportunities and be a part of collective lo
 cal impact for a cleaner\, greener Burlington.\n\n2026 COMMUNITY CLEAN UP 
 GREEN UP SUPPORTERS\n\nLEAD SUPPORTERS\n\n(https://www.burlington.ca/en/in
 dex.asp)\n\n(https://otf.ca/)\n\nCOMMUNITY PARTNER\n\n(https://portal.club
 runner.ca/144/)\n\nTREE SPONSOR\n\n(https://burlingtoncentre.ca/sustainabi
 lity/)\n\nLEAF SPONSORS\n\n(https://rsales.ca/)\n\n(https://bunzlcanada.ca
 /)\n\nSEED SPONSOR\n\n(https://djb.com/) DJB Chartered Professional Accoun
 tants\n\nHelp BurlingtonGreen (a Registered Canadian Charity)\, continue t
 o provide impactful\, community-based environmental programs.\nDonations o
 f all amounts are greatly appreciated.\n\n(https://www.burlingtongreen.org
 /donate/) DONATE TODAY!\nURL: https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/green
 -up-community-tree-planting-event/
URL:https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/green-up-community-tree-plantin
 g-event/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Join us at the beach this summer!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260701T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260907T000000
DTSTAMP:20260729T080830Z
UID:79abb066-8970-55db-adf2-8f2db26ab1e5
DESCRIPTION:Our team is leading eco-activities and sharing resources at ou
 r (https://maps.google.com/?cid=5383717800969327865&g_mp=CiVnb29nbGUubWFwc
 y5wbGFjZXMudjEuUGxhY2VzLkdldFBsYWNlEAMYASAF&hl=en-CA&source=embed) Eco Hub
  (1094 Lakeshore Rd) throughout the summer.\n\nPop by for a variety of eco
 -awareness\, advocacy\, and action opportunities\, such as nurdle hunts\, 
 button making\, microplastic beach clean ups\, seed ball making\, our popu
 lar Eco-Trivia game\, and more!\n\nYou can also visit our (https://www.bur
 lingtongreen.org/bgs-pollinator-garden/) pollinator garden to learn about 
 the importance of pollinators like bees and butterflies\, and how they sup
 port healthy ecosystems.\n\nFollow us on (https://www.facebook.com/burling
 tongreen) Facebook\, (https://www.instagram.com/burlingtongreenenv/) Insta
 gram\, (https://www.linkedin.com/company/burlingtongreen-environmental-ass
 ociation/) LinkedIn or (https://bsky.app/profile/burlingtongreen.bsky.soci
 al) Bluesky for updates on our week and weekend programming\, 10 am – 4 
 pm (weather permitting).\nURL: https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/join
 -us-at-the-beach-this-summer/
URL:https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/join-us-at-the-beach-this-summe
 r/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Volunteer Celebration & AGM
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260612T000000
DTSTAMP:20260729T080830Z
UID:7f4f47a9-5344-571c-9f96-ac299ab74487
DESCRIPTION:All community members are invited to our brief Annual General 
 Meeting\, followed by an informative opportunity to discover and celebrate
  the valued impact of volunteering with BurlingtonGreen\, including volunt
 eer recognitions.\n\nJoin us for this special opportunity to mark our trem
 endous shared community impact over the past year\, and celebrate the wond
 erful community members who volunteer with BurlingtonGreen.\n\nThere will 
 be opportunities to connect informally and learn about rewarding volunteer
  opportunities for individuals\, families and groups with BurlingtonGreen.
 \n\n6:30 pm – 7:00 pm: Annual General Meeting\n7:00 pm – 8:00 pm: Disc
 over and Celebrate Volunteer Impact\nLocation: Centennial Hall\, Central L
 ibrary\, 2331 New Street ( (https://www.google.com/maps?cid=70695379237929
 28824) map)\n\nComplimentary seed packets and refreshments will be availab
 le.\n\nPlease RSVP by completing the form below.\n\nLet us know you’ll b
 e there!\n\nWe invite you to check out our rewarding (https://www.burlingt
 ongreen.org/volunteer/) volunteer opportunities and join us in recognizing
  (https://www.burlingtongreen.org/our-supporters/) our valued supporters.\
 nURL: https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/volunteer-celebration-agm-202
 6/
URL:https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/volunteer-celebration-agm-2026/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Join Spring Eco Action at the Beach!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260516T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260516T120000
DTSTAMP:20260729T080831Z
UID:8a3f5579-0d94-5239-b209-c4bcb61cc34a
DESCRIPTION:The (https://portal.clubrunner.ca/144) Rotary Club of Burlingt
 on Central and BurlingtonGreen invite you to a FREE Spring Eco Action at t
 he Beach event\, with opportunities including a guided walk to learn about
  birds in this sensitive ecosystem\, an all-ages teaching about the Four S
 isters of Mother with WhiteEagle\, and a collective beach clean up to care
  for our beautiful shoreline.\n\nHosted by: Rotary Club of Burlington Cent
 ral & BurlingtonGreen\n\nWhen: Saturday\, May 16th\, 2026\n\nWhere: Burlin
 gton Beach – meet at BG’s Eco-Hub (https://www.google.com/search?q=109
 4+Lakeshore+Rd.\,+Burlington\,+ON+L7S+1A7&shndl=40&source=sh/x/loc/geo/m1/
 1&kgs=f095e45074c197e0) (1094 Lakeshore Road)\n\nNote: Please register in 
 advance\, using the form below.\n\nJoin with fellow community members to t
 ake action for our environment and learn about local nature with a meaning
 ful day of community engagement!\n\nEvent Highlights and Schedule:\n\nBird
  Walk (8:30 am – 9:30 am)\nIn celebration of spring bird migration and W
 orld Migratory Bird Day\, join us for a free guided bird walk to learn abo
 ut the interesting birds that live at the beach and those that migrate thr
 ough our area each year\, with avid birder Dave Tourchin of (https://birdf
 riendlyhamiltonburlington.wordpress.com/) Bird Friendly Hamilton-Burlingto
 n. Bring binoculars if you have them (there will be a few pairs available 
 to lend out). A BFHB information table will also be onsite all morning\, w
 here you can learn about ways you can help conserve birds.\n\nThe Four Sis
 ters of Mother – A Teaching by WhiteEagle (9:30 am – 10:00 am)\nBring 
 your beach blanket or chair to join together with other community members 
 for story telling\, reflection and connection led by WhiteEagle\, Indigeno
 us Healer.\n\nBeach Litter Clean-up (10:00 am – noon)\nLearn about plast
 ic pollution and help remove litter\, plastic waste and debris from Burlin
 gton Beach\, ensuring a healthier habitat for wildlife and a cleaner shore
 line for all to enjoy.\n\nFun Eco Activities for all ages (10:30 am – no
 on)\nGet hands-on with fun\, drop-in family-friendly activities such as ma
 king pollinator-friendly seedballs\, sharing your eco actions as part of o
 ur interactive campaign\, and nurdle discovery activity.\n\nWhy join?\nCon
 nect with like-minded community members\, learn valuable locally-informed 
 insights into reducing your carbon footprint\, and have fun while giving b
 ack to local nature!\n\nThis FREE event is open to all Burlington communit
 y members who care about the environment and is a local community offering
  as part of (https://www.epicdayofservice.org/) Rotary International’s E
 pic Day of Service 2026.\n\nLet’s build our awareness and take action to
  protect our local environment and the planet.\n\nActivities are outdoors\
 , rain or shine. Participant accessibility needs to be shared in advance w
 ith BurlingtonGreen\, please.\n\nSee you at the beach!\n\nUse the form bel
 ow to sign up for these exciting opportunities.\n\nUnpublished form\n\nTha
 nk you to the following for helping to make this event possible:\n\n(https
 ://birdfriendlyhamiltonburlington.wordpress.com/) 			 				 			 		\n\n			 	
 			 			 		 			 				 			 		 			 				 			 		\n\n(https://portal.clubrunner.c
 a/144/)\n\n(https://www.burlington.ca/en/index.aspx)\n\n(https://otf.ca/)\
 n\n(https://burlingtoncentre.ca/sustainability)\n\n(https://rsales.ca/)\nU
 RL: https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/join-spring-eco-action-at-the-b
 each-2/
URL:https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/join-spring-eco-action-at-the-b
 each-2/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Get ‘EM by the Roots
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260530T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260531T000000
DTSTAMP:20260729T080830Z
UID:8c1f4a7f-a974-550b-80d6-b5cd0241e347
DESCRIPTION:Join Invasive Species Action Month when you sign up to partici
 pate in a morning of ‘digging in’ and getting dirty as we come togethe
 r with our friends at (https://portal.clubrunner.ca/144) Rotary Club of Bu
 rlington Central to improve biodiversity along a section of the (https://b
 rucetrail.org) Bruce Trail running through (https://www.burlington.ca/en/n
 ews/current-city-projects-and-construction/city-view-park.aspx) City View 
 Park.\n\nTogether we will tackle invasive (https://www.invasivespeciescent
 re.ca/invasive-species/meet-the-species/invasive-plants/buckthorn/) Buckth
 orn and (https://www.invasivespeciescentre.ca/invasive-species/meet-the-sp
 ecies/invasive-plants/garlic-mustard/) Garlic Mustard plants.\n\nThis is a
  great opportunity to learn about the negative effects of invasive plant s
 pecies\, while helping to support native plants and wildlife in our local 
 greenspace.\n\nLet’s make a difference together!\n\nPlease note:\n\n* Ga
 rlic Mustard removal requires bending and or kneeling to carefully remove 
 plants by hand at ground level. This activity is open to ages 10 and above
 . Children ages 10-13 must be accompanied by an adult.\n\n* Buckthorn remo
 val involves a number of tasks such as digging with shovels\, operating ex
 tractigators\, and carrying removed bushes/branches.\n\nSpace is limited f
 or this event with advance registration required.\n\nDiscover more (https:
 //www.burlingtongreen.org/spring-into-action/) fun and rewarding opportuni
 ties this Spring to take ACTION for the planet\, locally.\n\nCheck out our
  fabulous line-up of (https://www.burlingtongreen.org/donate/sponsorship-o
 pportunities/) sponsorship opportunities and (https://www.burlingtongreen.
 org/live-green/businesses-and-community-groups/) facilitated volunteer opp
 ortunities for businesses and community groups – be a part of collective
  local impact for a cleaner\, greener Burlington.\n\n			 				 			 		 			 	
 			 			 		\n\nEvent funding provided by:\n\nCO HOST\n\n(https://portal.clu
 brunner.ca/144/)\n\n(https://www.burlington.ca/en/index.aspx)\n\n(https://
 otf.ca/)\n\nHelp BurlingtonGreen (a Registered Canadian Charity)\, continu
 e to provide impactful\, community-based environmental programs.\nDonation
 s of all amounts are greatly appreciated.\n\n(None) DONATE\nURL: https://w
 ww.burlingtongreen.org/events/get-em-by-the-roots/
URL:https://www.burlingtongreen.org/events/get-em-by-the-roots/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Decoding Bird Names with Bob Bell
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260312T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260312T210000
DTSTAMP:20260729T080831Z
UID:b7ac7e65-e686-5f86-ae55-4a5666ad877e
DESCRIPTION:Thank you to everyone who attending this event. A recording of
  the webinar is available (https://www.burlingtongreen.org/programs/nature
 -friendly-burlington/feathered-friends/) here.\n\nDate:Thursday\, March 12
 th\, 2026\nTime: 7pm\nLocation: Zoom Webinar\n\nRegister for this FREE eve
 nt further below.\n\nJoin us for an interactive and educational birding we
 binar with Bob Bell\, aka The Birder Bob\, on Thursday\, March 12th\, from
  7:00–8:15 pm on Zoom.\n\nHave you ever wondered why some bird names are
  so confusing? Bob will demystify them in a fun and approachable way. You
 ’ll also get a chance to test your bird ID skills with photos\, songs\, 
 and calls.\n\nBook Giveaway!\n\nThanks to Bob’s generosity\, one webinar
  participant will win a copy of his book (https://www.hancockhouse.com/pro
 ducts/out-of-the-lyme-light-and-into-the-sunlight) Out of the Lyme Light a
 nd Into the Sunlight: Birding as Therapy for the Chronically Ill.\n\nA gre
 at evening for curious beginners and seasoned birders alike.\n\nBob has pr
 eviously given six talks for BurlingtonGreen\, which are available for fre
 e to view on our YouTube channel:\n\n(https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OS0P
 27zRMKk) Backyard Birding with Bob Bell\n\n(https://www.youtube.com/watch?
 v=6YId2j9hC0Y) Out of the Lyme Light: Wellness Through Birding with Bob Be
 ll\n\n(https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=R4t30gOYpMI) Introduction to Birdin
 g in Burlington and Hamilton with Bob Bell\n\n(https://www.youtube.com/wat
 ch?v=-1zcW08eINo) The Mystique of Owls: An Introduction to Owling in Ontar
 io with Bob Bell\n\n(https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TclIU5DIGlk) The Wond
 erful World of Warblers with Bob Bell\n\n(https://youtu.be/Msyd5VaeaX0?si=
 tFJ9AmRg8XDQnno7) Mysteries of Migration Birding Webinar with Bob Bell\n\n
 Bob would be delighted to have you follow his book and birding activity\, 
 by sending a friend request (https://www.facebook.com/TheBirderBob/) on Fa
 cebook\, or by following him on (https://bsky.app/profile/thebirderbob.bsk
 y.social) Bluesky and (https://www.instagram.com/thebirderbob/) Instagram.
 \n\nBob’s book\, “ (https://www.hancockhouse.com/products/out-of-the-l
 yme-light-and-into-the-sunlight) Out of the Lyme Light and Into the Sunlig
 ht: Birding as Therapy for the Chronically Ill” can be bought locally at
  (https://burlington.wbu.com/) Wild Birds Unlimited and (https://www.diffe
 rentdrummerbooks.ca/) A Different Drummer Books in Burlington\, and at (ht
 tps://kingwestbooks.com/) King W. Books in Hamilton. It is also available 
 online from Amazon\, Indigo\, or directly (https://www.hancockhouse.com/pr
 oducts/out-of-the-lyme-light-and-into-the-sunlight) from the publisher.\n\
 nMore about Bob Bell:\n\nBob Bell spent 35 years as a mineral exploration 
 geologist before retiring to Ancaster in 2015. He quickly discovered that 
 the area\, with its multitude of habitats and environments\, was fantastic
  for birding.\n\nBob is passionate about sharing the joy of birding with p
 eople of all skill levels and enjoys introducing them to the huge variety 
 of beautiful birds that can be seen in the Hamilton and Burlington areas.\
 n\nHe hopes that his passion will inspire others to take in the sights and
  sounds of nature that surround us\, and that this interest will translate
  into support and protection of local birds.\n\nLearn more about Burlingto
 nGreen’s (https://www.burlingtongreen.org/programs/nature-friendly-burli
 ngton/) Nature Friendly Burlington Program.\n\nSign up for our monthly (ht
